course: dictionary
lesson: 851
title: Betray and the clues of trust
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To betray someone means to hurt them by being disloyal, so they can no longer trust you. The words around the word give you the clues. «Sam's older brother spent the birthday money Grandma posted and said "It never came, mate."» Then «Sam felt betrayed by his own brother, which was worse than losing the money.» Sam did not lose the money by accident. His brother lied, and that is why Sam felt let down by someone he trusted.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Does "Sam felt let down by someone he trusted" fit? Yes, so betrayed means hurt by someone's disloyalty. Telling a secret, breaking a promise or helping an enemy can all be betrayal.
explain: Betray can also mean showing a feeling without meaning to. «Her shaking hands betrayed her fear.» Her hands did not mean to tell anyone, but they showed how scared she was. The clue is "shaking", which is a sign of fear.
explain: Being honest with a trusted adult is not betrayal. «Telling a grown-up about harm is not betraying a friend; it is getting them help.» Telling a grown-up keeps your friend safe.
fact: To betray someone means to hurt them by being disloyal, such as telling their secret or breaking a promise.
fact: «Betrayed» means let down by someone you trusted.
fact: To betray your country means to help its enemies.
fact: To betray a feeling means to show it without meaning to, as in «Her shaking hands betrayed her fear.»
fact: Telling a trusted adult about harm or danger is not betraying a friend. Phrases to know: betray a secret, betray someone's trust, feel betrayed.
exercise: «Sam felt betrayed by his own brother, which was worse than losing the money.» What does betrayed mean here? | Angry at the post office | Happy because he got a present | Bored by the birthday party | *Let down by someone he trusted
exercise: «Telling a grown-up about harm is not betraying a friend; it is getting them help.» Is telling a trusted adult about harm a betrayal? | Yes, it is always a betrayal | Only if it happens on a birthday | *No, it is getting your friend help | Yes, but only if your friend is older
exercise: «Her shaking hands betrayed her fear.» What does betrayed mean here? | Made her laugh out loud | *Showed her fear without meaning to | Hid her fear completely | Hurt her hands badly
exercise: Which is an example of betraying someone's trust? | Keeping their secret safe | Saying sorry when you have been wrong | *Telling their secret to other children | Helping them carry their bag
test: «To betray your country is to help its enemies.» What does it mean to betray your country? | *To help its enemies, which is betraying your country | To help its enemies | To paint its flag | To give your country a present
test: Mia says, «My best friend shared my secret with the whole class. I feel betrayed.» What does feel betrayed mean? | Very tired after a long day | Excited to make new friends | Proud of myself | *Hurt because someone I trusted let me down
exam: «A new friend doesn't betray an old one.» What does this sentence tell us? | Old friends should never be trusted | A new friend should stay loyal to an old friend, not be disloyal | A new friend is always better than an old one | *A new friend should stay loyal to an old friend
